# Slack. Geometry taken off Slack's own SVG, the one the flatpak ships at
# /var/lib/flatpak/exports/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/com.slack.Slack.svg, after an
# earlier version drawn from memory had every bar on the wrong axis.
#
# Each colour is a bar plus a knob set perpendicular to it. Blue runs left across the top
# left with its knob above, green runs up the top right with its knob to the right, yellow
# runs right along the bottom right with its knob below, red runs down the bottom left with
# its knob to the left. The shape is exactly 4-fold symmetric, every arm maps onto the next
# under a 90 degree turn.
#
# Proportions come straight from the original. Its bars are 63 units of a 300 unit mark,
# which is 2.9 px here, so 3 px bars with blocks at 4..6 and 9..11 and the centre cross at
# 7..8 is the honest translation rather than a guess.
#
# The centre cross is filled white instead of left open. The knobs are what make that work,
# they close the cross off, and without them it runs out to the border and the outline rule
# puts four stray c0cbdc pixels at its ends. A white fill is also not a hole, so the outline
# does not eat into it and the cross keeps the width it is drawn at.
#
# Colours are the nearest ramp steps to the brand, 2ce8f5, 25d366, feae34 and e43b44, each
# outlined with its own darker step. Every one except the red is already another icon's
# fill, cyan is vscode, green is whatsapp, yellow is folder. Deliberate exception to the
# collision rule, since Slack is the only multicoloured icon in the set and the combination
# identifies it even though no single arm does.
A 2ce8f5
B 25d366
C feae34
D e43b44
E ffffff
F 0099db
G 0f7a44
H f77622
I a22633
